{
  "id": "u02-l04",
  "unit": "u02-pronouns",
  "title": "Yes/no, who & this/that",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "To ask a yes/no question, add **কি** (*ki*) right after the subject: **আপনি কি শিক্ষক?** 'Are you a teacher?' Nothing else changes.\n\nSpelling: **কি** (short ি) is the question marker; **কী** (long ী) means 'what'. They sound the same: **এটা কী?** 'What is this?' vs **এটা কি বাংলা?** 'Is this Bengali?'\n\n**এটা / ওটা** = this / that (এ 'this', ও 'that', plus -টা 'the thing'). **কে** = who: **উনি কে?** 'Who is he/she?'\n\nTwo languages: **বাংলা** (*bangla*, Bengali) and **ইংরেজি** (*ingreji*, English).",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "ki-q",
      "bn": "কি",
      "tr": "ki",
      "en": "(yes/no question marker)",
      "notes": "Turns a statement into a yes/no question: আপনি কি শিক্ষক? Usually comes right after the subject. Short ি — compare কী 'what'."
    },
    {
      "id": "ke",
      "bn": "কে",
      "tr": "ke",
      "en": "who"
    },
    {
      "id": "eta",
      "bn": "এটা",
      "tr": "eta",
      "en": "this",
      "notes": "এ 'this' + classifier -টা. Spoken BD also এইটা (eita)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ota",
      "bn": "ওটা",
      "tr": "ota",
      "en": "that",
      "notes": "ও 'that' + classifier -টা. Spoken BD also ওইটা (oita)."
    },
    {
      "id": "bangla",
